course: dictionary
lesson: 10808
title: Vary: to be different, or to change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To vary means to be different from each other, or to keep changing. «Dogs vary in size more than any other kind of mammal.» Dogs are not all the same size: some are tiny and some are huge.
explain: «Goodbyes vary, like "See ya", "Cheers", "Take care" or "Catch you later".» People say goodbye in different ways, so the words change from person to person and from place to place.
explain: To vary something on purpose means to change it so it is not always the same. In a varied diet you eat lots of different foods, and in a science fair test you vary only one thing at a time.
fact: Vary is a verb: vary, varies, varied, varying.
fact: To vary means to be different from each other, or to change.
fact: «Prices vary from shop to shop» means each shop may charge a different price.
fact: «The weather varies a lot» means it changes often.
fact: In a fair test, a variable is a thing you change on purpose so you can see what makes the difference.
exercise: «Dogs vary in size more than any other kind of mammal.» What does vary mean here? | Sleep all day | *Are different from each other | Make a loud noise | Are always the same size
exercise: «Goodbyes vary, like "See ya" and "Cheers".» What does vary tell you about goodbyes? | Goodbyes are always sad | Everyone says exactly the same word | *People say goodbye in different ways | Nobody says goodbye
exercise: In a fair test, what should you vary? | *Only one thing | Everything at once | The time of day, every time | Nothing at all
test: Your teacher says, «Vary your exercises.» What should you do? | Stop doing exercise | Write them down only | Do the same exercise again and again | *Change them so they are different
test: «The weather varies a lot.» What does varies mean? | It stays the same all week | It is always cold | *It changes often | It has no weather at all
exam: Fill the gap: «Prices ___ from shop to shop.» | sleep | happen | shrink | *vary
